  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;OSNABRÜCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osnabrück is a German city that has been twinned with Evansville since 1962, fostering a strong bond through cultural and economic exchanges."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVANSVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Evansville is a city in Indiana, USA, twinned with Osnabrück since 1962, engaging in various forms of cultural, educational, and economic exchanges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Evansville is a city in the United States involved in a sister city relationship with Rosh HaAyin."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WOLFGANG GRIESERT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wolfgang Griesert is the Mayor of Osnabrück and a key figure in the city's sister city relationship with Evansville."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLOYD WINNECKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lloyd Winnecke is the Mayor of Evansville and a key figure in the city's sister city relationship with Osnabrück."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF SOUTHERN INDIANA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Southern Indiana has a strong exchange program with Osnabrück University, facilitating student and faculty exchanges."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OSNABRÜCK UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Osnabrück University participates in exchange programs with the University of Southern Indiana, enhancing academic and research collaborations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SISTER CITIES INTERNATIONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sister Cities International is a non-profit organization that facilitates international partnerships, supporting the Osnabrück-Evansville relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROSH HAAYIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rosh HaAyin is a city in Israel involved in a sister city relationship with Evansville."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rosh HaAyin is a city in Israel that has a twinning relationship with Evansville since 2003, promoting cultural, economic, and educational exchanges."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VANDERBURGH COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vanderburgh County, Indiana, is the county seat of Evansville, which is part of the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROSH HAAYIN-EVANSVILLE CULTURAL FESTIVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Cultural Festival features performances by Israeli and American musicians, dancers, and artists, promoting cultural exchange."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVANSVILLE-ROSH HAAYIN BUSINESS FORUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Evansville-Rosh HaAyin Business Forum brings together business leaders from both cities to discuss trade and investment opportunities, fostering economic ties."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROSH HAAYIN-EVANSVILLE STUDENT EXCHANGE PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Student Exchange Program allows 20 students from each city to participate in a month-long exchange program, enhancing educational opportunities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Germany is the country where Osnabrück is located, playing a role in the international partnership with Evansville."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israel is the country where Rosh HaAyin is located, playing a role in the international partnership with Evansville."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VANDERBURGH COUNTY, INDIANA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vanderburgh County, Indiana, is the county where Evansville is located, part of the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF EVANSVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Evansville's Center for Economic Development has conducted studies on the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF INTERNATIONAL RELATIONS AND DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Journal of International Relations and Development is a scholarly journal that publishes research on international relations and development issues."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Journal of International Relations and Development published a study on the impact of the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF EVANSVILLE CENTER FOR ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Evansville Center for Economic Development has conducted studies on the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"University of Evansville Center for Economic Development is an institution that conducts research and provides resources for economic development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISRAELI BUSINESS LEADERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Israeli business leaders proposed the idea of twinning Rosh HaAyin and Evansville in 2001, initiating the partnership."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAYORS OF OSNABRÜCK AND EVANSVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mayors of Osnabrück and Evansville signed a formal agreement to establish the twinning relationship in 2003."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2004 ROSH HAAYIN-EVANSVILLE CULTURAL FESTIVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2004 Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Cultural Festival promoted cultural exchange between the two cities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2007 EVANSVILLE-ROSH HAAYIN BUSINESS FORUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2007 Evansville-Rosh HaAyin Business Forum discussed trade and investment opportunities between the two cities."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2012 ROSH HAAYIN-EVANSVILLE STUDENT EXCHANGE PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2012 Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Student Exchange Program allowed students from both cities to participate in a month-long exchange program."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A. COHEN AND J. SMITH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. Cohen and J. Smith are authors of a study on the impact of sister city relationships on international trade."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. Cohen and J. Smith published a study on the impact of sister city relationships on international trade in the Journal of International Relations and Development."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;J. JOHNSON AND M. DAVIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"J. Johnson and M. Davis are authors of a study on the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Twinning."&lt;SEP&gt;"J. Johnson and M. Davis published a study on cultural exchanges in the Rosh HaAyin-Evansville twinning relationship in the University of Evansville Center for Economic Development report."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SISTER CITY RELATIONSHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sister City Relationships refer to a formal agreement between two cities in different countries to promote cultural, educational, and economic exchanges."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE ROSH HAAYIN-EVANSVILLE TWINNING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rosh HaAyin-Evansville Twinning is a specific instance of a sister city relationship between Rosh HaAyin and Evansville."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONTH-LONG EXCHANGE PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A month-long exchange program is mentioned as a reference for participating in sister city relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL TRADE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"International trade is discussed as an impact of sister city relationships according to the study by A. Cohen and J. Smith."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURAL EXCHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cultural exchanges are highlighted as a key aspect of sister city relationships according to the study by J. Johnson and M. Davis."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0167</data>
    </node>
